error[NK2105]: You're using `t` again, but it was passed to `push`, which keeps it.
  --> tests/a_view_of_a_kept_text_parameter_suggests_a_copy.nika:5:5
   |
 5 |     return t.trim()
   |     ^
   |
   = note: `t` is a `String`, so it's handed over itself, not a copy. Nikaia never copies behind your back, because a copy costs as much as the value is large.
   = note: Numbers, `bool`s, `scalar`s and views would be fine: they're copied.
   = help: If both need it, hand over a copy: `t.clone()`.
error[NK2302]: `f` hands back a view of `t`, which it takes by value, so the data is gone when the call returns.
  --> tests/a_view_of_a_kept_text_parameter_suggests_a_copy.nika:5:5
   |
 5 |     return t.trim()
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
   = note: `t` is moved into `f` and ends with it; a view of it can't outlive the call.
   = help: Where the body keeps `t`, keep a copy instead (`t.clone()`), so `t` is lent and the view points into the caller's text; or hand back text of its own: write `.clone()` on the view handed back.
1 view kept past the call that was given it
